Anna: It was great, but I felt a bit nervous in the morning.
Tom: Me too. I got lost trying to find the science lab.
Anna: Did you join any clubs yet?
Tom: Yes, I joined the badminton club. We meet in the gym on Tuesdays.
Anna: That sounds fun. I chose the drama club because I love acting.
Tom: Nice! Standing on the stage must be exciting.
Anna: It is. I hope this year will be a wonderful new start.', '汤姆问安娜高中第一天怎么样;安娜说很棒,但早上有点紧张;汤姆也是,还找科学实验室时迷了路;安娜问汤姆加了社团没;汤姆加了羽毛球社,周二在体育馆活动;安娜选了戏剧社,因为爱表演;汤姆说登台一定很激动;安娜希望这一年是美好的新开始。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How did Anna feel in the morning of her first day?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A bit nervous.","Very bored.","Quite angry.","Completely calm."]},{"q":"What problem did Tom have on the first day?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["He forgot his bag.","He got lost finding the science lab.","He missed the bus.","He lost his timetable."]},{"q":"Which club did Tom join?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The badminton club.","The drama club.","The debate club.","The music club."]},{"q":"Why did Anna choose the drama club?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Because it is easy.","Because she loves acting.","Because her friend chose it.","Because it meets in the gym."]},{"q":"What does Anna hope for this year?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A long holiday.","Fewer lessons.","A wonderful new start.","A new school."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required1', 'U1', 'fltrp');
It is a great chance to get to know the school and meet others.
On that day, you can walk around the campus and find your classrooms.
Teachers introduce the clubs and after-school activities you can join.
If you keep an open mind, you may even make some new friends.', '许多学校为新生举办迎新日;这是了解学校、结识他人的好机会;那天你可以在校园里走走,找到自己的教室;老师们会介绍可以参加的社团和课后活动;只要保持开放的心态,你甚至能交到新朋友。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who is the Orientation Day for?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only teachers.","Old students only.","Parents.","New students."]},{"q":"What can students do on that day?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Walk around the campus and find their classrooms.","Take a big exam.","Stay at home.","Leave school early."]},{"q":"What do teachers introduce?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The summer holiday plan.","The clubs and after-school activities.","The exam results.","The school history only."]},{"q":"What is one chance the day offers?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A chance to win money.","A chance to skip class.","A chance to get to know the school.","A chance to go home."]},{"q":"How might you make new friends, according to the talk?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["By staying silent.","By avoiding everyone.","By leaving early.","By keeping an open mind."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required1', 'U1', 'fltrp');
Ben: Good idea. There is so much to do that I feel under pressure.
Lily: First, let''s list the things we are going to do.
Ben: Okay. We need to read English, finish maths and practise for the debate.
Lily: Right. Now let''s decide how long each task will take.
Ben: We should do the most important one first, I think.
Lily: Agreed. And let''s do only one task at a time.
Ben: Great. With a clear plan, the weekend feels much easier.', '莉莉提议为周末做学习计划;本说事情太多,感到压力;莉莉建议先列出要做的事;本说要读英语、做数学、准备辩论;莉莉建议再决定每项花多久;本认为应先做最重要的;莉莉同意,并建议一次只做一件事;本说有了清晰的计划,周末轻松多了。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What do Lily and Ben want to make?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A weekend study plan.","A shopping list.","A travel plan.","A party invitation."]},{"q":"Why does Ben feel under pressure?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["He is ill.","There is so much to do.","He has no friends.","He lost his books."]},{"q":"What do they decide to do after listing the tasks?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Sleep first.","Go out to play.","Decide how long each task will take.","Forget the plan."]},{"q":"Which task does Ben think they should do first?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The easiest one.","The shortest one.","Any one at all.","The most important one."]},{"q":"How does Ben feel about the weekend with a clear plan?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It feels much easier.","It feels boring.","It feels longer.","It feels useless."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required1', 'U1', 'fltrp');
At first, you may struggle to write down every word.
But thinking is more important than copying everything.
Try to note only the key information, such as names and numbers.
This simple habit will help you understand and remember more.', '在高中,老师讲课往往很快;起初,你可能很难记下每个词;但思考比把每句话都抄下来更重要;试着只记关键信息,比如名字和数字;这个简单的习惯会帮你理解并记住更多内容。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What do teachers often do during lessons?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Stay silent.","Speak quickly.","Read very slowly.","Leave the room."]},{"q":"What may be difficult at first?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Finding the classroom.","Saying hello.","Writing down every word.","Reading a poster."]},{"q":"What is more important than copying everything?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Sleeping in class.","Talking to friends.","Drawing pictures.","Thinking."]},{"q":"What kind of information should you note?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Key information like names and numbers.","Every single word.","Nothing at all.","Only the date."]},{"q":"What will this habit help you do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Forget the lesson.","Understand and remember more.","Leave school early.","Write more slowly."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required1', 'U1', 'fltrp');
Mark: Of course. What would you like to know?
Kate: How can I deal with all these new challenges?
Mark: Keep calm and be prepared. Plan your time every week.
Kate: What if I fail a test at the start?
Mark: Don''t worry. If you fail, next time you can do better.
Kate: That''s really helpful. Thank you so much.
Mark: My pleasure. Just keep an open mind and enjoy your new start.', '凯特向一位学长马克请教建议;马克乐意帮忙;凯特问如何应对新挑战;马克建议保持镇定、做好准备、每周规划时间;凯特担心一开始考试失败;马克说别担心,失败了下次能做得更好;凯特很感激;马克叫她保持开放心态,享受新开始。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who does Kate ask for advice?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A new teacher.","Her mother.","A senior student.","A shopkeeper."]},{"q":"What does Kate want to know?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Where the gym is.","When the holiday starts.","Which club is best.","How to deal with new challenges."]},{"q":"What is Mark''s first piece of advice?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Keep calm and be prepared.","Give up early.","Copy others'' work.","Avoid all tests."]},{"q":"What does Mark say about failing a test?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["You should leave school.","Next time you can do better.","You should feel ashamed.","It can never happen."]},{"q":"What does Mark tell Kate to do at the end?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Stop asking questions.","Study less.","Keep an open mind and enjoy the new start.","Forget the advice."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required1', 'U1', 'fltrp');
Starting senior high may feel hard at the very first.
You meet new teachers and face many new challenges.
But if you stay calm and try your best, things get easier.
Remember to help your friends, and you will feel good too.', '人们常说,良好的开端是成功的一半;刚上高中可能会觉得艰难;你要遇见新老师,面对许多新挑战;但只要保持镇定、尽力而为,事情就会变得容易;别忘了帮助朋友,你自己也会感觉很好。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What do people often say about a good beginning?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It is a waste of time.","It never matters.","It is always easy.","It is half the success."]},{"q":"How may starting senior high feel at first?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Hard.","Very boring.","Completely easy.","Quite sad."]},{"q":"What do new students have to face?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["No lessons at all.","Many new challenges.","Only old friends.","A long holiday."]},{"q":"What helps things get easier?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Giving up quickly.","Staying angry.","Staying calm and trying your best.","Doing nothing."]},{"q":"What happens when you help your friends?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["You lose your time.","You feel worse.","You make them sad.","You feel good too."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required1', 'U1', 'fltrp');

-- ===== 6) 写作 1篇 =====
DELETE FROM public.junior_writing_prompts WHERE publisher='fltrp' AND volume='required1' AND unit='U1';

I can hardly believe my first week at senior high is over! The thing I remember most is my first English lesson. The teacher asked us to introduce ourselves one by one. With butterflies in my stomach, I breathed deeply and said my name. To my surprise, it was the same as the teacher''s, and everyone laughed. I felt embarrassed at first, but his kind words made me feel relaxed. Now I feel more confident, and I am really looking forward to the year ahead.', '【15 分制】A 档(13-15):五要素齐全、组织有条理、语言准确多样;B 档(10-12):要点较全、少量错误;C 档(7-9):要点偏少、句型简单;D 档(0-6):内容不完整、错误多。', '["The thing I remember most this week is my first English lesson.","With butterflies in my stomach, I breathed deeply and said my name.","His kind words made me feel a lot more relaxed.","I am really looking forward to the year ahead."]'::jsonb, '[{"wrong":"His words made me to feel relaxed.","correct":"His words made me feel relaxed.","note":"make sb do sth,后接不带 to 的动词原形。"},{"wrong":"I felt very nervously before the speech.","correct":"I felt very nervous before the speech.","note":"feel 是系动词,后接形容词作表语,不用副词。"},{"wrong":"The teacher gave to me a useful book.","correct":"The teacher gave me a useful book.","note":"give sb sth 双宾语结构,间接宾语前不加 to。"}]'::jsonb, '【高中第一周日记结构】
日期一行:Friday, 8 September
第1句 点题:The thing I remember most this week is …
第2-3句 经过:The teacher asked us to … . With … , I … .
第4句 转折感受:I felt … at first, but … made me feel … .
第5句 收尾期待:Now I feel … , and I am really looking forward to … .', 2, 'required1', 'U1', 'fltrp');

